You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot 3.2 service migrating to Java 21 Virtual Threads (`Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()`) experiences severe throughput degradation and carrier thread starvation under heavy load. Thread dumps reveal the following component implementation:

java
@Service
public class RemoteBillingService {
    private final Object lock = new Object();
    private final RestClient restClient;

    public RemoteBillingService(RestClient restClient) {
        this.restClient = restClient;
    }

    public BillingResponse executeBilling(BillingRequest request) {
        synchronized (lock) {
            return restClient.post()
                    .uri("/api/v1/charge")
                    .body(request)
                    .retrieve()
                    .body(BillingResponse.class);
        }
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where database records are intermittently committed even when downstream validation fails, resulting in partial state mutations. You locate the following service implementation in the codebase:

java
@Service
public class OrderFulfillmentService {
    private final OrderRepository orderRepository;

    public OrderFulfillmentService(OrderRepository orderRepository) {
        this.orderRepository = orderRepository;
    }

    @Transactional
    public CompletableFuture<Void> processOrderAsync(Order order) {
        return CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
            orderRepository.save(order);
            if (order.isInvalid()) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("Invalid order payload detected");
            }
        });
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an internal gateway deployed on Kubernetes (assigned 2 CPU cores) experiences extreme latency spikes and thread starvation across all services. The gateway fetches user information concurrently using the following code:

java
public CompletableFuture<UserDashboard> getDashboard(String userId) {
    CompletableFuture<UserProfile> profileFuture = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
            () -> userClient.fetchProfile(userId));
    CompletableFuture<List<Order>> ordersFuture = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
            () -> orderClient.fetchOrders(userId));

    return CompletableFuture.allOf(profileFuture, ordersFuture)
            .thenApply(v -> new UserDashboard(profileFuture.join(), ordersFuture.join()));
}
